        "answer": "Create horizontal list with args2..9, spacing4, final true; align Left, set class/id/sound/update flag and enqueue. Construct and attach backing, Spacer, keyPrompt, button, Spacer3, label and Spacer2 with exact immediate geometry/style literals. Store separately owned keybind callbacks, register Label links, input_source_changed and LastInput refresh, four state predicates, model validations and setState hook. Install close hook. Optional PreLoadFunc is called late at206 (no PostLoadFunc call). If IsPC call SetupButtonPromptForPC, UseLocalHeight and SetupHideContextualPromptPC; otherwise only UseLocalHeight. Return self; no child effects duplicated. Read supplied model; non-nil update key shortcut prompt using self/controller/value, wrap AlreadyLocalized, set keyPrompt.keybind text. Get self model; if truthy get it again and select Label; if truthy call exact keyPrompt.keybind.__KeyBind pointer. No fallback text. Forward model/controller to button:setModel. Read Label model; non-nil LocalizeToUpperString and set label text. Disabled predicate checks root model enum flag_disable_prompts; only if truthy checks IsGamepad; only if truthy checks flags bpf_contextual; return last value. Enabled predicate checks root model enum flag_enable_prompts, then IsGamepad, then flags bpf_contextual, each short-circuited. DisabledPC predicate starts root enum flag_disable_prompts. If truthy require not IsGamepad AND not ShouldHideButtonPromptForPC, else set false; then check bpf_contextual; if truthy check IsPC; return last value. EnabledPC predicate starts root enum flag_enable_prompts. If truthy require not IsGamepad AND not ShouldHideButtonPromptForPC, else false; then bpf_contextual and conditional IsPC; return last value. Read the supplied model without a nil guard and call captured menu:updateElementState with the exact captured widget and model_validation table in source_trace (menu, controller, modelValue and literal modelName preserved). No explicit return; state dispatcher effects remain opaque. Fill event.menu from captured menu only when existing value false/nil, then update captured self with same event; no nil check. Read the supplied model without a nil guard and call captured menu:updateElementState with the exact captured widget and model_validation table in source_trace (menu, controller, modelValue and literal modelName preserved). No explicit return; state dispatcher effects remain opaque. Read the supplied model without a nil guard and call captured menu:updateElementState with the exact captured widget and model_validation table in source_trace (menu, controller, modelValue and literal modelName preserved). No explicit return; state dispatcher effects remain opaque. setState hook: default+mouse/keyboard disables mouse button, hides supplied element and updates PC contextual model; otherwise mouse/keyboard enables, shows element and updates model; otherwise default+gamepad disables and hides self; otherwise gamepad enables and shows self. Other inputs do nothing. Repeated helper calls and element/self difference are preserved.",
